agraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object with match() and reset() methods"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getprogress","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getProgress"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getProgress: () => number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"match","children":[{"type":"text","value":"match"}]},{"type":"code","value":"match: (event) => boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"event","children":[{"type":"text","value":"event"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyboardEvent"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reset"}]},{"type":"code","value":"reset: () => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const matcher = createSequenceMatcher(['G', 'G'], { timeout: 500 })\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  if (matcher.match(event)) {\n    console.log('Sequence matched!')\n  }\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"sequence","text":"sequence","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"platform","text":"platform?","level":4},{"id":"timeout","text":"timeout?","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"getprogress","text":"getProgress","level":3},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"match","text":"match","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"event","text":"event","level":5},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"reset","text":"reset","level":3},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createSequenceMatcher(sequence, options?): object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [sequence-manager.ts:704](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/sequence-manager.ts#L704)\n\nCreates a simple sequence matcher for one-off use.\n\nThis is a low-level helper that does not support ignoreInputs, target,\nor other HotkeyOptions. Callers must handle input filtering themselves\nif attaching to document.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n[`HotkeySequence`](../type-aliases/HotkeySequence.md)\n\nThe sequence of hotkeys to match\n\n### options?\n\nOptions including timeout\n\n#### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\n#### timeout?\n\n`number`\n\n## Returns\n\n`object`\n\nAn object with match() and reset() methods\n\n### getProgress\n\n```ts\ngetProgress: () => number;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`number`\n\n### match\n\n```ts\nmatch: (event) => boolean;\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### event\n\n`KeyboardEvent`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n### reset\n\n```ts\nreset: () => void;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst matcher = createSequenceMatcher(['G', 'G'], { timeout: 500 })\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  if (matcher.match(event)) {\n    console.log('Sequence matched!')\n  }\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createSequenceMatcher\ntitle: createSequenceMatcher\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createSequenceMatcher(sequence, options?): object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [sequence-manager.ts:704](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/sequence-manager.ts#L704)\n\nCreates a simple sequence matcher for one-off use.\n\nThis is a low-level helper that does not support ignoreInputs, target,\nor other HotkeyOptions. Callers must handle input filtering themselves\nif attaching to document.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n[`HotkeySequence`](../type-aliases/HotkeySequence.md)\n\nThe sequence of hotkeys to match\n\n### options?\n\nOptions including timeout\n\n#### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\n#### timeout?\n\n`number`\n\n## Returns\n\n`object`\n\nAn object with match() and reset() methods\n\n### getProgress\n\n```ts\ngetProgress: () => number;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`number`\n\n### match\n\n```ts\nmatch: (event) => boolean;\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### event\n\n`KeyboardEvent`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n### reset\n\n```ts\nreset: () => void;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst matcher = createSequenceMatcher(['G', 'G'], { timeout: 500 })\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  if (matcher.match(event)) {\n    console.log('Sequence matched!')\n  }\n})\n```\n"}
